1
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:08,190
 Today I'm going to tell you the story of a great dabbler.

2
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:12,300
 The only man who could say that he was in a real sense universal.

3
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:18,740
 Some people have jokingly suggested that Leonardo da Vinci, he's the one, was surely one of my ancestors.

4
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,980
 Well, in all modesty, I won't comment.

5
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,000
 Still, when I contemplate his last statue, I wonder.

6
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,140
 Here we are in Italy at the end of the 15th century.

7
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:30,060
 The Quattrocento, as they called it.

8
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,760
 Italy was a group of little states.

9
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:34,600
 The most brilliant Florence, governed by Lorenzo de' Medici.

10
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:36,000
 Lorenzo the Magnificent.

11
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:39,160
 He saw art and science as a means to power, and he protected artists.

12
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,740
 The invention of gunpowder and cannons had made fortified castles obsolete.

13
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:44,640
 They were turned into country residences.

14
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:48,080
 Gutenberg had printed his first book, and Columbus would soon discover America.

15
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:51,100
 Artists are pampered, except for Leonardo da Vinci, the greatest.

16
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:53,340
 He will leave ungrateful Florence for Milan,

17
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,180
 where he will be under the protection of the city master,

18
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,460
 Ludovic Sforza, called the Moor.

19
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:07,340
 I insist, Uncle, that my 12th birthday celebrations are the biggest ever seen in Milan.

20
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:10,430
 Jan Gagliazzo, my dear nephew.

21
00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:12,740
 You know I never refuse you anything.

22
00:01:13,570 --> 00:01:14,110
 Now go.

23
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:25,990
 I'd say, the young man is showing a bit of arrogance.

24
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,810
 That's because he's really the Duke.

25
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:31,270
 Enough!

26
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:37,510
 My poor arrogant nephew, he may not live long.

27
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:39,790
 And his advisor wouldn't be around long either.

28
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:43,370
 Really, Ludovic, everybody knows you're in charge.

29
00:01:43,650 --> 00:01:45,070
 You do with the kid what you like.

30
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:49,180
 Still in such a situation, yes?

31
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:53,640
 Lord, a Signor Leonardo da Vinci request an audience.

32
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:57,220
 Ah, that nut. The mad one. Send him away.

33
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:02,220
 Yeah, send him away. I've a prodigy who'd do much better.

34
00:02:02,610 --> 00:02:07,250
 But Lorenzo de' Medici says that his knowledge of art is beyond questioning, Ludovic.

35
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:13,830
 As you say. But this da Vinci, he says, just listen to what he's written.

36
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:15,450
 Most illustrious signore.

37
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:17,940
 Oh, yes. Listen.

38
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:21,720
 I have projects for bridges that are sturdy and light, easy to transport.

39
00:02:22,470 --> 00:02:24,250
 And for the siege of a stronghold.

40
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:29,290
 I know how to design and build bridges, battering rams, ladders for scaling walls, etc, etc.

41
00:02:29,510 --> 00:02:33,750
 I have plans for mortars that can rain down stones like a hailstorm.

42
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:39,360
 I have shoes that can walk on water, diving suits for moving underwater.

43
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:41,570
 Clearly he's crazy, that's all.

44
00:02:41,970 --> 00:02:45,830
 I can build tanks that will destroy an enemy army and sustain no damage.

45
00:02:46,490 --> 00:02:48,960
 He's crazy. He's crazy as a bed bug.

46
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,580
 He can deliver large catapults and machines of war.

47
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:55,120
 He's a good architect. He's a musician and a sculptor.

48
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,200
